rag-tuda uses the third-party models, libraries and data listed here. Each keeps its own licence and terms; this file names
them and says what was checked. "Not read" means the licence text was not available locally when this file was written:
read it at the source before redistributing anything.

Models served by the model servers and the indexer (downloaded from Hugging Face, pinned by revision in the profile)
  Snowflake/snowflake-arctic-embed-m-v2.0   the embedder          licence stated on its model card: apache-2.0
  BAAI/bge-reranker-v2-m3                    the reranker          licence stated on its model card: apache-2.0
  docling-project/docling-layout-heron       PDF layout (docling)  licence stated on its model card: apache-2.0
  docling-project/docling-models             PDF tables (docling)  licence stated on its model card: cdla-permissive-2.0

Answer models named by the model cards in models/cards/ (pulled by Ollama or served by Groq or vLLM; none is shipped here)
  Qwen3.5 4B (s-qwen3.5-4b)                  Apache License 2.0 (the LICENSE file of its Hugging Face snapshot)
  Qwen3 4B Instruct 2507, Qwen3.6 35B-A3B, Qwen3.8 27B, Qwen3 235B-A22B Instruct 2507 FP8 (vLLM example)
                                             licences not read; see each model's Hugging Face page
  Gemma 4 E4B and 31B                        licence not read; see Google's model page and terms
  gpt-oss 20B and 120B                       licence not read; see OpenAI's model page
  Models reached through Groq are also bound by Groq's terms for its hosted service.

Libraries vendored in web/page/vendor/ (versions, sources and integrity hashes in web/page/vendor.json)
  showdown 2.1.0         MIT
  dompurify 3.4.16       (MPL-2.0 OR Apache-2.0)
  d3 7.9.0               ISC
